{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.open_per_partition_witnessed_empirically","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.open_per_partition_witnessed_empirically","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L195-L220","doc":"The OpenPerPartitionConjecture is **CONDITIONALLY** witnessed\nby the empirical max-|μ| selector — but the predicate\n`isMaxEigSpectrum` is itself decidable only via eigenvalue\nevaluation, not via a closed-form substrate rule. Closing the\nstructural identification of `isMaxEigSpectrum` is the open\nR&D part flagged in `rem:per-partition-k-lambda-rule`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.OpenPerPartitionConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.OpenPerPartitionConjecture","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L171-L191","doc":"**The open structural form.** The conjecture that there exists\na substrate-derivable `isMaxEigSpectrum` predicate such that the\n`candidateRule` based on it closes the AME binding for all atoms\n`{D, T, ³He}` within `eps = 0.05` (= 5%).\n\nThis is the surviving open form of `conj:brane-tower-z-habiro`\nafter PR #638 refuted scalar and per-eigenvalue forms and PR #639\nshowed the per-partition relaxation is sufficient.\n\n\"Substrate-derivable\" excludes per-atom retuning: the same\n`isMaxEigSpectrum` predicate must apply to all atoms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.tritium_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.tritium_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**Theorem.** The per-partition rule collapses Tritium's\nbrane-tower magnitude to `|tower| < 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.deuteron_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.deuteron_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L151-L159","doc":"**Theorem.** The per-partition rule collapses Deuteron's\nbrane-tower magnitude to `|tower| < 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.he3_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.he3_per_partition_tower_magnitude_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L139-L149","doc":"**Theorem.** The per-partition rule collapses ³He's brane-tower\nmagnitude to `|tower| < 2`, demonstrated by direct numerical\nbracket on the witness-derived constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.perPartitionTowerSigned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.perPartitionTowerSigned","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L133-L137","doc":"**Per-partition tower under the candidate rule.** With the\ndominant partition taking `k_λ = 1` and others `k_λ = 2`,\nthe total tower equals `domContribK1(λ_dom) + nonDomSumK2(λ_dom)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.nonDomSumK2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.nonDomSumK2","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L125-L131","doc":"Sum of non-dominant partition contributions at k = 2 (computed\nfrom PR #639 witness data). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.domContribK2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.domContribK2","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L116-L123","doc":"Dominant-partition contributions at uniform k = 2 (per PR #639\nwitness). The witness shows these as the failure-driving\nterms in the uniform-k tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.domContribK1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.domContribK1","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L107-L114","doc":"Dominant-partition contributions at uniform k = 1 (per PR #639\nwitness). All three atoms have their dominant partition's\ncontribution near zero at k = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.he3DominantPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.he3DominantPartition","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L104-L105","doc":"³He dominant partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.tritiumDominantPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.tritiumDominantPartition","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L101-L102","doc":"Tritium dominant partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.deuteronDominantPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.deuteronDominantPartition","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Deuteron dominant partition under the per-partition rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.PerPartitionRecovery","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.PerPartitionRecovery","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**Propositional content:** the per-partition `k_λ` rule\nrecovers the empirical binding `B_target` to within relative\nerror `eps`, given `phiProj` computed via per-partition\ntruncation.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b: `phiProj` is an EXPLICIT input (not ∃-bound).\nCaller must produce a concrete numerical value from the\noperator-valued brane tower under the rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.candidateRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.candidateRule","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L73-L81","doc":"The empirical \"max-|μ| selector\" rule, encoded abstractly:\n`k_λ = 1` if `λ` is the maximum-eigenvalue-magnitude\npartition in the spectrum of `ρ_λ(β_atom)`; `k_λ = 2`\notherwise. The actual `isMaxEigSpectrum` predicate is\ndecidable only via numerical eigenvalue evaluation; this\nLean encoding records the SHAPE of the rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.KLambdaRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.KLambdaRule","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L69-L71","doc":"A per-partition truncation assignment for a fixed strand count.\nMaps each partition `λ ⊢ n` to a truncation level `k_λ ∈ ℕ_≥1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerPartitionKLambda.Partition","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerPartitionKLambda.lean#L65-L67","doc":"A partition of `n` represented as a weakly-decreasing sequence\nof positive natural-number parts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}